{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3Mw8dKKNLrzH9XuteYK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run test:ssr`, `npm test` and `npm run size` pass\n\nTicket 05 is finished and committed in four commits, and all the gates pass: `npm test` 293/293, `npm run test:ssr` 80/80, `npm run size`, and lint.\n\nThe first attempt did the right work but failed only because another worktree's test run was using port 8123. None of its changes were in this worktree, so I redid them here. That port collision happened again during this run; waiting and retrying fixed it, and I added a note about it to AGENTS.md.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n1. **Server** (`src/htm.ts`): non-empty component children are now wrapped in `<!--[c-->` … `<!--]-->`. A component with no children gets no markers. The static-page exact-string assertions in the SSR suite were not touched and still pass.\n2. **Browser** (`src/htm.browser.ts`): when looking for a host's children, `_range` now looks for the `[c` marker instead of the region marker. `_close` treats both `[` and `[c` as opening markers when matching the closing one by depth. Hosts the browser creates also wrap their children in `<!--[c-->`, so later updates find the children the same way. `_skip` needed no change.\n3. **Tests** (`test/index.ts`):\n   - A new adoption test covers a component whose render has a reactive region before its children. Before the fix, the button's listener was not bound.\n   - A second test covers nested hosts and regions inside the children.\n   - The existing children fixture now uses `<!--[c-->`.\n4. **Docs**: updated CONTEXT.md (**Reactive region**), ADR-007 (corrected decision text plus a dated Notes section) and AGENTS.md.\n\n**Nested-host test:** it passed on its first run because the depth counting arrived with item 2. To check that it can fail, I broke the code twice and restored it after each. Removing the depth counting made it fail, and so did letting `_range` look inside nested hosts. Simply mounting over the server HTML can't show the case where the children are found to end too early, so the test also re-runs a region around the host, which forces the children to be updated.\n\n**Size:** the browser templater is 4.57 kB against its 4.6 kB limit, so I didn't raise the limit. Later tickets that add code to the browser templater will probably need to.\n\n**Not run:** `test:hydration` and the e2e suite. The spec says the example doesn't build until the finding-1 ticket lands, so they would fail regardless of this change.\n\nNotes for the next run are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":599,"cache_read_input_tokens":91448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":599},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"069db358-592f-4b78-8ac7-2a31cc4c3e85","uuid":"187bceb9-f0b2-4346-af5a-4119bae3d87a","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:05:43.157Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Mw8MCtoJuAWKF9dU5V"}
